  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>What do you notice? What do you wonder?</para>
<para>\(y = 1.5x+22.7\)</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para><figure><media alt="Scatter plot."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/bf2fe432333358279dea1ef61899da13956c741b"/></media></figure></para>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
    <para>Things you may notice:</para>
    <list>
      <item>More people generally means more noise.</item>
      <item>At around 65,000 people, there are three different noise levels.</item>
      <item>The equation of the line is given.</item>
    </list>
    <para>Things you may wonder:</para>
    <list>
      <item>Where is the origin?</item>
      <item>Why are all the points not on the line?</item>
      <item>What can we do with this?</item>
    </list>
     
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
</content>
